From: 0xFFshell <0xffshell@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:03:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] humanize: carry the look through the hostile run

The lean between the movement rotation and the aim machinery was covered
only as single offers: GazeAheadTest pins the lean's own bounds and
ApproachLookTest pins the job's guards, but nothing drove a coherent
stream of them through the spin-up, the reaction and the carry over long
hostile runs.

The fuzz harness now keeps a walk direction that persists across ticks,
offers onto it the way the executor's running ticks do (the line ahead
twice, the job's block once, ramped like the approach with a hostile few
starts heavier than any real ramp), and asserts over every draw: a
clicked target is leaned never, an offered lean goes no further off the
walk than the cap, and the pitch takes no more than the weight's share.
Three focused tests pin what the draws can only sample: a coherent look
settles onto the leaned line and turns with it when the offer turns, the
stand-aside returns the rotation untouched mid-lean (identity, not
tolerance), and a flapping offer at full weight and the cap's amplitude
can neither carry the head past the lean plus the carry nor freeze it.

Teeth by mutation, two pins: dropping blockInteract from GazeAhead#lean
fails nothingSurvivesTwentyThousandHostileTicks and
theLookStandsAsideForAClickMidLean on the stand-aside; dropping the
sixty-degree clamp fails the same run on the deviation and the flapping
test's cap self-check. Full suite: 41 classes, 341 tests, 0 failures.
